# Trivy ignore list. Every entry needs a justification and an expiry (exp:) so it is re-evaluated.

# http-cache-semantics <=4.2.0 (no patched release): cross-user disclosure via max-stale in shared caches.
# Not affected: only used at build time (astro remote-image cache for the static site, and got ->
# cacheable-request in electron-builder for Electron downloads). No shared multi-user HTTP cache.
CVE-2026-93748 exp:2027-01-03

# picomatch <=4.0.7 (no patched release): ReDoS through single-branch repeated extglobs (+(*), +(*a)).
# GitHub withdrew GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf on 2026-11-18 (the maintainer disputes it: globs are regexes, so
# never compile untrusted ones), but the CVE and GitLab advisory still list it. Drop this entry once
# Trivy stops reporting it.
# Not affected: Loxel's own matchers take globs only from the user's settings, built-in defaults and
# language servers' fixed capabilities; yaml-language-server only gets the user's yaml.schemas (its
# SchemaStore catalog is off); astro-ls and the build tools (astro, vite, electron-builder) glob fixed
# patterns. The one project-controlled input, dependency-cruiser's `workspaces` matching in the
# code-analysis binary, is patched out at build time (packages/code-analysis/build.ts, Patch 5).
CVE-2026-112366 exp:2027-01-17
